WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.372
Empowerment expands people's ability to influence and carry out their work.

2
00:00:04.572 --> 00:00:07.563
Participation invites input into decisions.

3
00:00:07.763 --> 00:00:14.269
Neither works well when the invitation hides fixed decisions or leaves people without information and resources.

4
00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:20.580
Cedar Crossing's project group can propose the display sequence within agreed space and access requirements.

5
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.912
The manager explains which choices the group may make, which need approval, and where to get help.

6
00:00:26.112 --> 00:00:31.186
The group also needs relevant skills, usable information, time, and a clear result.

7
00:00:31.386 --> 00:00:37.978
A small decision agreement can identify purpose, participants, decision authority, process, and follow-up.

8
00:00:38.178 --> 00:00:43.504
Different decisions may call for consultation, delegated choice, voting, or consensus.

9
00:00:43.704 --> 00:00:49.060
Define the process before relying on it; a vote and consensus are not interchangeable.

10
00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:54.123
Self-management means taking on management responsibilities within an agreed scope.

11
00:00:54.323 --> 00:00:57.621
It does not mean that support and accountability disappear.

12
00:00:57.821 --> 00:01:06.024
Evaluate whether participation improves both the work and people's ability to contribute, and change arrangements when the evidence shows a problem.
